-- Fixture rows that give the system console realistic data to render in a development stack:
-- applications, projects, members, and pending invites for the kinotic-test organization, plus
-- worker nodes and workloads in every state for the orchestrator views. Development-only — the
-- e2e suites assert against exact kinotic-test contents and must not see these rows.

-- Applications owned by kinotic-test

-- Projects across the applications above; repoConnectionStatus varies so each state renders

-- Organization members (no credentials — fixture identities never log in);
-- one disabled member so the Members table renders the Disabled status

-- Org-level pending invites (no applicationId). Far-future expiresAt keeps them visible:
-- the pending-invite queries filter out expired rows

-- Worker nodes. Allocated figures equal the sum of the non-stopped workloads placed on each
-- node below, so capacity bars agree with the workload table. status is an OBJECT column and
-- INSERT takes only scalar values, so these seed as the entity default (ONLINE).

-- Workloads covering every WorkloadStatus, both kinotic-test and platform (no organizationId)
-- scope, and a PENDING row with no nodeId (not yet placed)
-- autoRemove false: the VM disk is kept, so the console offers Restart on this stopped row
